YALNPN (Yet another long night playing Nethack)

This character was a randomly created one.  I found several bones files
from my own deaths that helped a great deal.  This was my fourth
ascension, and possibly the easiest.

I had identify, and plently of other nice spells.  With AC - 47 and
around 400 hit points, I was in good shape.  Polying amulets is nice
too, I had 2 or 3 amulets of life saving that I never needed.

Doompa was using a +7 Firebrand for most of the game.  First time with
a character using that, and it is very nice.  I also used = of free
action and !oParalysis to take out several baddies including Asmodeous
and Yeenoghu, and Death.

I kept a +5 robe the entire game, while wearing and removing a shield
of reflection when needed.

This character alchemized many potions into full healing; maybe around
25 potions worth.  The bones files provided some good healing potions
too.

The closest I came to death was in Ludios.

I cleared out the whole level except for an orange dragon, and another
humanoid with a /of Sleep.  Somehow, I had lost my sleep resistance,
and I was down to 36 hit points.  Praying didn't help.  I would fall
asleep, and watched helplessly as my hitpoints went up and down.  My
heart was pounding.

Luckily, I survived, and killed off the opponents.  I then killed an
elf soon enough to acquire the resistance again. No close calls after
that.

I magic mapped all of Gehennom with scrolls and magic.  Makes it much
easier.  Double Trouble Rodneys fell to /oDeath.  Planes were a breeze.

All in all, a very fun ascension, full of wishing, polying, and
genoing.  And my girlfriend came up with YALNPN.

